.\" Adapted for BNU from the GNU Coreutils 9.11 manual page; see doc/README.md.
.TH ECHO "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
echo \- display a line of text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B echo
[\fI\,SHORT-OPTION\/\fR]... [\fI\,STRING\/\fR]...
.br
.B echo
\fI\,LONG-OPTION\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Echo the STRING(s) to standard output.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#echo-n'\fB\-n\fP\X'tty: link'
do not output the trailing newline
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#echo-e'\fB\-e\fP\X'tty: link'
enable interpretation of backslash escapes
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#echo-E'\fB\-E\fP\X'tty: link'
disable interpretation of backslash escapes (default)
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/echo#echo--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/echo#echo--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
.PP
If \fB\-e\fR is in effect, the following sequences are recognized:
.TP
\e\e
backslash
.TP
\ea
alert (BEL)
.TP
\eb
backspace
.TP
\ec
produce no further output
.TP
\ee
escape
.TP
\ef
form feed
.TP
\en
new line
.TP
\er
carriage return
.TP
\et
horizontal tab
.TP
\ev
vertical tab
.TP
\e0NNN
byte with octal value NNN (1 to 3 digits)
.TP
\exHH
byte with hexadecimal value HH (1 to 2 digits)
.PP
Your shell may have its own version of echo, which usually supersedes
the version described here.  Please refer to your shell's documentation
for details about the options it supports.
.PP
Consider using the \fBprintf\fP(1) command instead,
as it avoids problems when outputting option\-like strings.
